+> Historical record. Commands, controls and test policies below may be retired. Use ../TESTING.md and ../ROADMAP.de.md for current guidance.
+
+# Riftline – Wünsche des Eigentümers und Plan
+
+As of 27.10.2026, with 3.57.0. New entries are written in English (the owner's wish since 03.10.2026).
+
+## 04.11.2026 — Shattered Core landmark and repository identity
+
+The Shattered Core gains a fractured crown beyond the arena barrier, giving the weakest-rated biome
+a stable silhouette without changing collision or combat space. Repository, Pages and package links
+now point to `Anton037/Riftline`, and the GitHub setup guide uses the current visual-audit command.
+
+## 04.11.2026 — repository cleanup and faster delivery
+
+The desktop browser flow covers the complete run cycle. The touch flow focuses on landscape
+input. Pages runs the Node checks and builds the deployment. Browser checks run on pull requests.
+The browser probe interface keeps only its current consumers' fields. Unused audio helpers and
+the retired Crucible soundtrack implementation are removed. Old save data stays supported.
+
+## 03.11.2026 — fresh test foundation (supersedes the policy below)
+
+Following the owner's request to remove and rebuild the tests, the historical browser chains,
+per-release self-test and golden catalogs are removed. The replacement uses Node's built-in runner:
+ten unit contracts and two desktop/touch flows. Default flows run live simulation and UI with GPU draws
+suppressed; real pixel rendering and visual/audio review are explicit commands. PRs and deployments
+use one bounded gate, without change planners or hidden extended suites. This deliberately reduces
+coverage; offline recovery, long sessions and device-specific comfort still need manual acceptance.
+
+## 03.11.2026 — tests matched to risk (same 3.61.0 update)
+
+The owner explicitly asked to simplify all tests, especially the slow deep test, and remove unnecessary work.
+`docs/TESTING.md` replaces the previous always-run-everything policy. The normal gate retains save/simulation,
+data/package and real-player smoke coverage. CI selects audio, gameplay, offline and full-biome checks from changes.
+The audio test drops subjective FFT/style rankings, separates the historical self-test, and closes a fresh browser
+per small sound chunk/place. Pure music budgeting no longer allocates unrendered native sources; real-node parity
+is checked for all six places. Two overlapping screenshot scripts and the duplicate release-check chain are removed.
+Full UI/E2E, old regressions, art review, soak/fuzz and sound analysis remain explicit tools rather than mandatory
+work on every small update. Removed-setting assertions are updated to the current UI rather than restoring controls.
+
+## 03.11.2026 — visual consistency and full-biome review (3.61.0)
+
+The current request is a whole-game review with consistent criteria, led by the unequal biome graphics.
+`docs/VISUAL-REVIEW-3.61.md` records the rubric, findings, measured render costs and validation limits.
+
+- Phase 2 is implemented: all six weather profiles and prop emission rates are named data in
+  `src/data/atmosphere.js`. Base emission rates stay the same; particle sizes vary within a small range.
+  Atmosphere now yields under particle pressure and stops adding particles above 30% pool occupancy.
+  This intentionally replaces the earlier “match counts within 10%” gate with a combat-reservation gate.
+- Readability/material pass across all six floors: broken, snow-buried ice fractures; worn Core tiles with
+  sparse lit seams and quieter decorative runes; lower marsh vein contrast; finer wet asphalt and glass
+  grain; calmer molten bounce and narrower glass joints. Hazard timing and warning geometry stay intact.
+- Phases 4/5 are partially addressed by batching compatible opaque static siblings by material. Animated
+  objects, instanced vegetation and translucent surfaces keep their own identity and sorting. Transparent
+  bosses are deliberately excluded, so the earlier universal 7–10-mesh target is not claimed as achieved.
+- The landscape phone boss bar moves between the sticks so it no longer crosses the boss or the wave/combo stack.
+- `npm run audit:visual` captures all six biomes and bosses with a fixed run seed on PC and landscape touch.
+  The existing biome/attack screenshot suites also visit every biome; the Flats now has its own attack stage.
+- No engine migration or new progression mechanics are needed for these findings. A real-device gameplay,
+  audio listening and GPU timing pass remains necessary before calling the whole game release-ready.
+
+## 28.10.2026 — biomes, enemies and effects: the overhaul, scoped (after 3.59.0)
+
+The owner asked for a biome, enemy and effect overhaul. This is the plan, grounded in what is actually
+asymmetric today, in the order it should be done. Each phase has a gate; nothing here is "make it prettier".
+
+**What is measured, not guessed**
+
+- **Ambient particles are per-place hand code.** `rlAmbient` in `src/render/biome-visuals.js` is a `switch` on
+  `biome.id` with the numbers written inline: the vault emits 34 flakes/s (was 42, cut in 3.44.0), the marsh
+  9 spores plus 4 fireflies plus the reed wind, the club 22 ash plus 11 embers (raised in 3.54.0). Every one of
+  those was tuned by eye, one release at a time, and nothing in the file states the intent — so the next change
+  is another guess. That is the real defect: not the densities, the fact that they are incomparable.
+- **Enemies arrive identically.** All 25 types have their own silhouette, animation, family death voice
+  (`RL_DEATH_FAMILY`, 25/25 mapped) and a kill burst tinted by `enemyDefs[type].color` — but `spawn` drew one
+  ring and one burst of one size for every type (`renderer.js`, `case "spawn"`): the colour was the type's own,
+  the shape was the same for all 25. Phase 1 fixes that; the rest of the phase is the family flourish.
+- **Bosses are 20–33 meshes each** (AUDIT.md M7), the largest single draw-call cluster left after 3.59.0.
+
+**Phase 1 (S) — a spawn that says what arrived.** Tint the spawn ring by the enemy's own colour and give the
+family a shape: fast types land with a streak, armoured ones with a heavy ring, flyers with a small vertical
+puff. Reuses `emit`/`ring` only, so no new per-frame draw calls. Gate: `npm run screens` per place, and a
+`selftest` assertion that every type in `enemyOrder` has an arrival shape.
+
+**Phase 2 (M) — the ambient table.** Move the per-place numbers out of the `switch` into a data table
+(rate, colour, vertical drift, size, drag per place) so a reader can compare two places at a glance and a
+reviewer can see a density change in the diff. Gate: the 3.58.0 screenshots matched within 10 % particle
+count per place.
+
+**Phase 3 (M) — wind-ups.** The field guide promises "chargers telegraph, then ram"; check every damaging
+attack for a wind-up of at least 0.25 s with a family sound, and give the ones without one a tell. Gate:
+`selftest` walks the enemy table and asserts each damaging attack has a wind-up field.
+
+**Phase 4 (L) — boss meshes.** Merge non-spinning parts per material (AUDIT.md M7: 20–33 → 7–10 draw calls).
+Gate: `npm run screens`, one image per boss per phase.
+
+**Phase 5 (L) — the prop merge left in AUDIT.md H3.** Same treatment for the marsh and the club, which still
+carry the most per-prop meshes.
+
+**Tooling, done here (3.60.0, no gameplay change):** `tests/balance.mjs` now draws its seeds from a fixed list
+and prints every seed's death wave, marking a row `noisy` when the spread reaches four waves. Before this, a
+run's rng was consumed by the spawn plan, so 3.58.0's one-enemy escort cut reseeded everything after wave 5 and
+moved the Rocket from wave 9 to wave 5 with no balance change behind it. A median of four chaotic runs was
+being read as a ranking; the spread says which rows can be read at all.
+
+## 27.10.2026 — project process back on `main` (3.57.0)
+
+`main` had lost its own process documents: they only existed on unrelated, re-rooted `claude/*` branches. They
+are restored here from those branches and reconciled with the code that is actually on `main`:
+
+- `CLAUDE.md`, `docs/DEVELOPMENT.md`, `docs/GITHUB.md`, `docs/STRATEGY-AUDIT.md` and this roadmap are back.
+  The release instructions in `CLAUDE.md`/`DEVELOPMENT.md` were corrected: the version and the build id move
+  together, and since 3.57.0 `src/build-info.json` is only a start-up identity, not a changelog (the build
+  writes just its version and build id to `dist/`).
+- `.github/workflows/nightly.yml` is recreated (it was referenced by `test.yml` but missing): the long checks
+  (E2E, short fuzz, world/run audits, screenshots as an artifact) plus the soak and the balance table.
+- The stale German `docs/QA-REPORT.de.txt` was deliberately **not** restored: it stops at 3.29.1 and would
+  contradict 27 releases of `main` (removed Ultra, five biomes, old boss names). The What's new tab
+  (`src/data/whatsnew.js`) is the player-facing history instead.
+
+The strategy section below is unchanged and still the owner's direction; the ranked improvements in
+`docs/STRATEGY-AUDIT.md` stay the plan.
+
+Diese Datei sammelt, was der Eigentümer sich gewünscht hat, was entschieden ist und
+welche Ideen noch offen sind. Zu Beginn einer Sitzung lesen, nach jeder Änderung des Plans aktualisieren (im selben PR).
+
+Leitgedanke des Eigentümers (steht auch in `CLAUDE.md`): alle Funktionen, Designs und Sounds passen organisch und
+dynamisch zusammen; das Spiel skaliert und wird schwerer, und sieht und klingt dabei schön. Neue Funktionen kommen
+mit Modell, Sound, Vorwarnung und Tests, nicht als nackte Mechanik. Der Eigentümer prüft Klang und Spielgefühl selbst:
+Musik und Balance sind von uns nur gemessen, nicht gehört oder gespielt.
+
+## Strategy audit of 10.10.2026 (on 3.29.1; read this first)
+
+**State.** Live: 3.29.1 (#58). The "CURRENT STATE" of 06.10.2026 below is older; 3.29.0 and 3.29.1 have been merged since.
+
+**The request.** The owner asked how to make Riftline a substantially better finished game: its look, sound, feel and
+performance, while friends can still open one link and play on ordinary phones, tablets and PCs. He asked for an
+investigation, decisions and a plan, not for changes. The full report, with the raw measurements and how to repeat them, is
+in `docs/STRATEGY-AUDIT.md`.
+
+**How it was judged.**
+
+- Screenshots and `renderer.info` of every biome (wave and boss) on PC and on a phone held sideways, taken from the live site
+  in software WebGL.
+- Offline renders of all 15 music tracks and 17 sound effects, measured for loudness, spectrum and stereo.
+- Simulation and audio cost measured in a crowded fight; the source code read.
+- **Not done:** no listening, no real devices, no play-testing.
+
+**Recommended direction.** Stay on three.js and the web, and change how the content is made:
+
+- **Made in Blender** (or licensed CC0) and imported as glTF: arena surroundings, landmarks and floors with **baked
+  lighting**. The arena is static and the camera nearly fixed, so baked light gives the better look at almost no runtime
+  cost (unlike Ultra).
+- **Kept in code:** simulation, combat effects, telegraphs, hazards' animation and the adaptive music.
+- **Not recommended:** Godot. Its web export runs only the reduced "Compatibility" renderer, its low-latency browser audio has
+  no effects, reverb or generated sound, the download is large, and it would mean a full rewrite. Babylon.js, WebGPU, an
+  engine switch or a backend bring no gain now.
+
+**Main findings.**
+
+1. **No sense of place.** Each arena is a flat patterned floor from above with box obstacles and nothing around the edge;
+   Blackout City does not read as a city.
+2. **Readability.** The biome skins paint the floor's pattern on enemies (`render/biome-visuals.js` `rlSkinMaterial`), so in
+   Ember Works and the Toxin Marsh enemies and bosses (Crucible, Hive Queen) blend into the floor. At their intro the bosses are
+   small, at the top edge, under the boss bar. The floors are busy, high-contrast graphics and fill about 70 % of the picture.
+3. **Sound (measured, not heard).**
+   - Music: 71–92 % of the energy is below 200 Hz, almost nothing above 8 kHz.
+   - Explosion, nova, rocket and scattergun: 86–96 % below 200 Hz.
+   - The mix is near mono, and the biomes have very similar tonal balance.
+   - Phone speakers barely play that range, so music and impacts mask each other in it. This is likely part of "the biomes
+     sound the same" and of the missing Osmos shimmer.
+4. **No frame cap on Auto and High** (`main.js`, `qualityPresets` `fps: 0`). 90/120 Hz Android phones render up to 120 fps,
+   about twice the GPU work and heat. Auto quality only steps down below 48 fps. The likely main GPU cost is the full-screen
+   procedural floor shader at DPR 1.5–2. All inferred from source, not measured on a device.
+5. **Light elsewhere (measured).** 405 KB download, 68–127 draw calls, 12k–47k triangles, 18–21 MB heap, 0.44 ms per
+   simulation step with 56 enemies.
+
+**First batch of work** (each a small PR):
+
+1. 60 fps cap by default on phones and tablets, Auto quality working to a pixel budget, and a `?perf` readout built on the run
+   monitor in `core/diagnostics.js`.
+2. A device baseline: the owner and 2–3 friends run `?perf` on their phones (a low-end and a 120 Hz Android, an older and a
+   current iPhone, an iPad, a laptop).
+3. A readability pass: skins as an accent only, calmer floors, bigger bosses that spawn away from the HUD bar, tips off the
+   play area on phones.
+
+**After that:** 4. Audio mix pass, procedural only: the bass reserved for impacts and the boss kick, one bright signature voice per biome,
+transient layers on impacts, wide but mono-safe beds, loudness targets in tests. The owner listens on a phone speaker and on
+headphones. 5. glTF asset pipeline (lazy load per biome, service-worker cache, size check in `build.js`). 6. **Blackout City pilot**: Blender kit, baked light, border and backdrop. Go or no-go judged on phones. 7. Recorded impact and ambience layers (1.5 MB at most, AAC or MP3). 8. A fullscreen button for Android and desktop, an iOS "Add to Home Screen" hint, a visible save export and import. 9. The rest of the biomes, one per PR; later perhaps authored boss models.
+
+**Decisions for the owner:**
+
+- The frame-cap default (also on desktop?).
+- Approve an art direction and send a reference picture.
+- iPhone silent switch: `audioSession.type = "ambient"` lets the switch mute the game; `playback` would ignore it.
+- A licence policy for assets.
+- Cloudflare Pages only as a preview link per pull request, to try changes on a phone before merging; GitHub Pages stays the
+  public link, and the leaderboard plan stays parked.
+- Which devices must run well.
+
+**Still unverified:** real heat and frame rate on phones; whether the mix sounds as bad as it measures; iPhone behaviour
+(silent switch, a phone call during a run, separate storage of home-screen apps); the feel of play.
+
+## Entschieden am 03.10.2026 (nach 3.5.0)
+
+Reihenfolge vom Eigentümer bestätigt: erst die schnellen Sachen und Fixes, dann die größeren Dinge. Jeder Punkt ein
